on Awards 2013\n  * Winner of Overall Excellence Award SCCI, Annual Corporate Report Award 2013\n  * Winner of the Outstanding Entrepreneurship, Award 2013 Asia Pacific Entrepreneurship Award 2013\n  * Winner of Malaysia HR Awards 2013, Employer of Choice Award (Bronze) & HR Leader of the Year Award (Bronze)\n  * Top 50 of Enterprise 50 (E50) Award 2013\n  * Winner of 1st Asian Company Secretary of the Year Recognition Awards 2013\n  * Green Building Index Award 2013 (Provisional) for Encorp Marina Puteri Habour\n  * Construction Industry Development Board Malaysia QLASSIC Certification 2013 for Magnolia Encorp Cahaya Alam (75% Rating)\n  * Construction Industry Development Board Malaysia QLASSIC Certification 2013 for Frangipani Encorp Cahaya Alam (81% Rating)\n\n### 2012\n\n  * Winner of Overall Excellence Award SCCI, Annual Corporate Report Award 2012\n  * Winner of the BrandLaureate’-s Most Eminent Brand Iconic Leadership Award, BrandLaureate Leadership Awards 2012\n  * Winner of Malaysia HR Awards 2012, Employer of Choice Award (Bronze) & HR Leader of the Year Award (Silver)\n  * Construction Industry Development Board Malaysia QLASSIC Certification 2012 for Camelia Encorp Cahaya Alam (83% Rating)\n\n### 2011\n\n  * Winner of the Highly Commended Award (Mixed-Used Development category for Malaysia), Asia Pacific Property Awards 2011\n  * Winner of Malaysia HR Awards 2011, Employer of Choice Award (Bronze) & HR Leader of the Year Award (Silver)\n\n### 2010\n\n  * Winner of The Edge PEPS Value Creation Excellence Award 2010 for non-residential category\n  * Top 27 of StarBiz ICR Corporate Responsibility Awards 2010--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMANAGEMENT DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS (https://smib.com.my/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/SMIB-AR-2025.pdf)\nciteturn312search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; The Group’s property development projects are in Ipoh and the car park sites are located at Kelana Jaya, Selangor while its wire factory is located in Tampoi, Johor.\nMANAGEMENT DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS\n\nThis management discussion and analysis should be read in conjunction with the audited financial statements of the Group and the Company for the financial period ended 30 September 2025.\n\nOVERVIEW\n\nThe Company is principally engaged in property and investment holding, trading, property development activities and the provision of management services while its subsidiaries are principally involved in property development, car park management and operation and manufacturing and trading of assorted wires.\n\nThe Group’s property development projects are in Ipoh and the car park sites are located at Kelana Jaya, Selangor while its wire factory is located in Tampoi, Johor.\n\nCHANGE IN FINANCIAL YEAR END\n\nOn 8 August 2025, the Company changed its financial year end from 30 June to 30 September. The audited financial statements of the Company for the preceding financial period were prepared for twelve (12) months from 1 July 2023 to 30 June 2024. Thereafter, the financial statements under review were for the fifteen (15) months period from 1 July 2024 to 30 September 2025. The change of financial year end applies to the Company and its subsidiaries.\n\nCORPORATE OBJECTIVES AND STRATEGIES\n\nThe Group’s main corporate objectives which were incorporated in the Group’s 3-Year Business Plan 2026 - 2028 are as follows:\n\n<visual_element id=\"e1\">\nCorporate objectives graphic with two numbered items:\n1 — “to sustain existing operations and turnaround to profitability by optimal utilisation of its available resources whilst meeting the needs of customers, employees and business partners”\n2 — “to identify business opportunities for long term growth”\n</visual_element>\n\nThe key aspect to the Group’s business sustainability is establishing continuous revenue streams while reigning in rising operating costs. The immediate priorities of the Board of Directors are:\n\nIdentifying New Land Bank\n\nThe challenge to the Group has always been finding suitable sizeable land banks at good locations. The Group will look for opportunities of acquiring lands with shorter holding periods and faster turnaround time. Joint ventures with suitable parties are also alternatives being pursued after the success of the Group’s first Joint Development project i.e. Pinnacle Kelana Jaya.\n\nFaced with slower global economic growth, exacerbated by weak property sentiments, conservative lending policies of financial institutions and higher stamp duty costs, the Management has adopted a cautious approach in considering potential land investments.\n\nIdentifying New Business\n\nBesides identifying suitable lands for development, the Group is also on the lookout to venture into new business that would help spur growth but again the slowdown in global and domestic demand has also increased business risks. The Group is adopting a more prudent and conservative approach with emphasis on market sentiments and risk analysis taking into consideration the changing business ecosystem and the greater focus on sustainability and environmental aspects.\n\n4 | SOUTH MALAYSIA INDUSTRIES BERHAD | ANNUAL REPORT 2025--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAbout SMI Berhad – SMIB (https://smib.com.my/about-smi-berhad/)\nciteturn312search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 days ago; The Group’s property development projects and car park sites are located in Kelana Jaya, Selangor and Ipoh while its wire factory is located in Tampoi, Johor.\n\n## Corporate Overview\n\nSouth Malaysia Industries Berhad (SMIB) is a public limited liability company incorporated and domiciled in Malaysia and it is listed on the Main Market of Bursa Malaysia Securities Berhad.\n\nSMIB is principally engaged in property and investment holding, trading, property development and the provision of management services while its subsidiary companies are principally involved in property development, car park management and operation, manufacturing and trading of assorted wires and leasing of premises.\n\nThe Group’s property development projects and car park sites are located in Kelana Jaya, Selangor and Ipoh while its wire factory is located in Tampoi, Johor. With the cessation of the Group’s cinema business in China in 2013, the operation in China is mainly the leasing of premises.\n\nDate of Incorporation  | :  | 27 March 1969\n\nStatus  | :  | Public Company listed on the Main Market of Bursa Malaysia Security Berhad on 2 August 1971\n\n* * *\n\nPrincipal Activities  | :  | Property and investment holding, trading, property development, and provision of management services.\n\nIssued and Fully Paid-Up Capital  | :  | RM244,239,167 Comprising 209,940,112 ordinary shares\n\n* * *\n\nBoard of Directors  | :  | Dato’ Dr Abdullah Bin Sepien DIMP, DJMK, SJMK\nChairman (Non-independent Non-Executive Director)Dato’ Zainuddin Bin Yahya DIMP\n(Independent Director)Dato’ Sri Mohd Mokhtar Bin Mohd Shariff\n(Independent Director)Puan Latifah Binti Abdul Latiff\n(Independent Director)\n\nShare Registrar  | :  | Bina Management (M) Sdn Bhd\nLot 10, The Highway Centre, Jalan 51/205\n46050 Petaling Jaya, Selangor.\nTel : (03) 7784 3922\nFax : (03)7784 1988\n\nRegistered Office  | :  | L2-02, 1 Medini Hub\nPersiaran Medini Utara 3,\nMedini Iskandar,\n79000 Nusajaya,\nJohor Darul Takzim Tel : (07) 8180 350\n\nCompany Secretaries  | :  | Ms. Wong Chee Yin, Ms. Tan Siew Chin\n\n* * *\n\nPrincipal Bankers  | :  | RHB Bank Berhad\nBank Islam Malaysia Berhad\n\n* * *\n\nAuditors  | :  | Messrs PKF PLT\n(AF 0911)\nLevel 33, Menara IMK,\nKompleks 1, Mont Kiara,\nNo.1, Jalan Kiara ,\n50480 Kuala Lumpur.Tel : 603 6203 1888\nFax : 603 6201 1880\n\nLiaison Personnel  | :  | Ms Yvonne Tan\nTel : (03) 2078 1522\nEmail : query@smib.com.my--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMANAGEMENT DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS (https://smib.com.my/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/SMIB-AR-2024.pdf)\nciteturn312search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.9 years ago; The Group’s property development projects are in Ipoh and the car park sites are located at Kelana Jaya, Selangor while its wire factory is located in Tampoi, Johor.\nMANAGEMENT DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS\n\nThis management discussion and analysis should be read in conjunction with the audited financial statements of the Group and the Company for the financial year ended 30 June 2024.\n\n### Overview\nThe Company is principally engaged in property and investment holding, trading, property development activities and the provision of management services while its subsidiaries are principally involved in property development, car park management and operation and manufacturing and trading of assorted wires.\n\nThe Group’s property development projects are in Ipoh and the car park sites are located at Kelana Jaya, Selangor while its wire factory is located in Tampoi, Johor.\n\n### Change in Financial Year End\nOn 31 March 2023, the Company changed its’ financial year end from 31 December to 30 June. The audited financial statements of the Company for the preceding financial period were prepared for eighteen (18) months from 1 January 2022 to 30 June 2023. Thereafter, the financial statements under review were for the twelve (12) months period from 1 July 2023 to 30 June 2024. The change of financial year end applies to the Company and its subsidiaries.\n\n### Corporate Objectives and Strategies\nThe Group’s main corporate objectives which were incorporated in the Group’s 3-Year Business Plan 2025 - 2027 are as follows:\n\n<visual_element id=\"e1\">\nCorporate objectives graphic with two numbered items:\n1 — “to sustain existing operations and turnaround to profitability by optimal utilisation of its available resources whilst meeting the needs of customers, employees and business partners”\n2 — “to identify business opportunities for long term growth”\n</visual_element>\n\nThe key aspect to the Group’s business sustainability is establishing continuous revenue streams while reigning in rising operating costs. The immediate priorities of the Board of Directors are:\n\n#### Identifying New Land Bank\nThe challenge to the Group has always been finding suitable sizeable land banks at good locations. The Group will look for opportunities of acquiring lands with shorter holding periods and faster turnaround time. Joint ventures with suitable parties are also alternatives being pursued after the success of the Group’s first Joint Development project i.e. Pinnacle Kelana Jaya.\n\nFaced with slowdown of the global economy, exacerbated by weak property sentiments and conservative lending policies of the financial institutions, the Management has adopted a cautious approach in considering potential land investments.\n\n#### Identifying New Business\nBesides identifying suitable lands for development, the Group is also on the lookout to venture into new business that would help spur growth but again the slowdown in global and domestic demand has also increased business risks. The Group is adopting a more prudent and conservative approach with emphasis on market sentiments and risk analysis taking into considerations the changing business ecosystem and the greater focus on sustainability and environmental aspects.\n\n4 | SOUTH MALAYSIA INDUSTRIES BERHAD | ANNUAL REPORT 2024--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSMIB – South Malaysia Industries Berhad (https://smib.com.my/)\nciteturn312search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 days ago; SMIB is principally engaged in property and investment holding, trading, property development and the provision of management services while its subsidiary companies are principally involved in property development, car park management and operation, manufacturing and trading of assorted wires and leasing of premises.\n\n##### Welcome to South Malaysia Industries Berhad\n\nSMIB is principally engaged in property and investment holding, trading, property development and the provision of management services while its subsidiary companies are principally involved in property development, car park management and operation, manufacturing and trading of assorted wires and leasing of premises.\n\n#### Our Core Business\n\n### Property & Township Development\n\n### Carpark Management & Operation\n\n### Property Investment & Holding\n\n### Assorted Wire Manufacturing\n\nCorporate Office\n\n13A Floor, Menara SMI\nNo 6 Lorong P.Ramlee\n50250 Kuala Lumpur\nTel : 03-2078 1522\nFax : 03-2072 1509--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nProperty Development – SMIB (https://smib.com.my/property/)\nciteturn312search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; ## Property Development\n\n## Property Development\n\n### Completed Project\n\n### On-going Project\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGroup Structure – SMIB (https://smib.com.my/group-structure/)\nciteturn312search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Anastoria Sdn Bhd (“Anastoria”)  | 14.04.75  | Malaysia  | 100  | Property development\n\n## Group Structure\n\nSubsidiary Companies\n   |     Incorporation  | Effective interest %  | Principal Activities\n       Date      | Country\nAnastoria Sdn Bhd (“Anastoria”)  | 14.04.75  | Malaysia  | 100  | Property development\nKam Kok Development Sdn Bhd  | 07.01.81  | Malaysia  | 100  | Property development\nSMI Cityhome Sdn Bhd (“SMIC”)  | 01.04.80  | Malaysia  | 100  | Property development\nSMI Wire Sdn Bhd  | 12.03.85  | Malaysia  | 100  | Manufacturing & trading of assorted wires\nSMI Multi Zone Sdn Bhd  | 13.12.2016  | Malaysia  | 100  | Car Park Management & Operation\nSMI Project Management Sdn Bhd  | 28.08.00  | Malaysia  | 100  | Dormant\n \nSubsidiary companies of Anastoria\n   |     Incorporation  | Effective interest %  | Principal Activities\n       Date      | Country\nLimpah Murni Sdn Bhd  | 23.02.95  | Malaysia  | 100  | Dormant--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCorporate Social Responsibility – SMIB (https://smib.com.my/news/)\nciteturn312search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; The Group supervises the safety conduct of its operations through the Operational Safety and Health (“OSHA”) committee, set up individually for both the Property and Wire Manufacturing Divisions.\n\n## Corporate Social Responsibility\n\nIn the social realm, South Malaysia Industries Berhad (SMIB) strives to not just engage with its employees, customers, and business partners, but also to foster high quality working relationship with local authorities, joint venture partners, suppliers, contractors, as well as agencies to create and deliver sustainable value to all its stakeholders.\n\nThe Group supervises the safety conduct of its operations through the Operational Safety and Health (“OSHA”) committee, set up individually for both the Property and Wire Manufacturing Divisions. OSHA meetings are held periodically to report and discuss any safety and health related risks, including formulation of action plans, if required.\n\nSMIB also emphasises on safety at workplace, providing employees with relevant personal protective equipment and periodic safety trainings to instil safety awareness. There were no major incidents recorded on work-related injuries or fatalities for the financial year ended 31 December 2017. The Group recognises the impact it may cause to the surrounding community of the property project sites.\n\nAs such, the Group has undertaken various efforts to minimize the impact, including not having night lights shone at the surrounding residences, constant reminders to truck drivers to reduce and limit the speed of their vehicles and notice boards set up which includes the contact numbers of project managers to allow complaints, if any, to be appropriately channelled and attended to."
